---
import GameLayout from '../../layouts/GameLayout.astro';
import GeographyQuiz from '../../games/geography/GeographyQuiz';
---
<GameLayout
  gamePageId="geography-capitals"
  title="Capital Cities Quiz – Countries & Capitals of the World"
  description="Free capital cities quiz. Name the capital of each country, or the country of each capital. Easy to hard, with notes on countries with multiple capitals."
  heading="Capital Cities Quiz"
  lead="Match countries with their capital cities — in both directions."
>
  <GeographyQuiz client:load preset={{ mode: 'capitals' }} />
  <Fragment slot="guide">
    <h2>Commonly confused capitals</h2>
    <p>The biggest or best-known city is often <em>not</em> the capital:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Australia — <strong>Canberra</strong>, not Sydney.</li>
      <li>Canada — <strong>Ottawa</strong>, not Toronto.</li>
      <li>Turkey — <strong>Ankara</strong>, not Istanbul.</li>
      <li>Brazil — <strong>Brasília</strong>, not Rio de Janeiro or São Paulo.</li>
      <li>Nigeria — <strong>Abuja</strong>, not Lagos.</li>
      <li>Switzerland — <strong>Bern</strong>, not Zurich or Geneva.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some countries split capital functions between cities; the explanation after each answer points this out where relevant.</p>
  </Fragment>
</GameLayout>
